  "quarantined_first_attempt": {
    "directory": "results/qualification/gate0_item1_fdir1_attempt1_harness_fault",
    "disposition": "Every record from that attempt is quarantined and unused, including the detached-pod records that did complete. The harness now kills parameter_bridge and counts it in the pre-run cleanliness guard, which is the same class of fix as the simulator-count guard added after the two-simulator contamination in the rotation sweep.",
    "fault": "The run harness never killed parameter_bridge, so a bridge outlived every case and they accumulated, while the same teardown deleted /dev/shm/fastrtps_* underneath the live ones. Gazebo stayed healthy and published /clock and odometry while no ROS participant could discover anything, and the first assembly case timed out waiting for readiness. Four bridges were alive at 323, 298, 274 and 26 seconds when it was caught."
